Title: Modern Warfare 4 Open Beta: Everything You Need to Know
URL: https://www.callofduty.com/uk/en/blog/2026/08/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-open-beta-everything-you-need-to-know
Published: 2026-08-21T00:00:00.000Z
Author: Call of Duty Staff
Highlights:
Across two action-packed weekends, experience Modern Warfare® 4's new Multiplayer modes, a playable Campaign mission, expanded movement systems, Ground War: Combat Outpost, Call of Duty®: Warzone™ Resurgence on the brand-new Zodiac map, and extensive Operator and Loadout customization.
...
## Campaign Mission: Entrenched
...
- NEW: For the first time in a Call of Duty Beta, experience a Campaign mission before launch.
- Join a large-scale ground assault to prevent the destruction of a vital nuclear power station.
- Experience Modern Warfare 4's dramatic cinematic Campaign action using the game's weapons, movement, and combat systems.
- Continue the fight when the full Campaign launches on October 23, or pre-order and play it one week earlier when Campaign Early Access begins on October 16.
...
For the first time in a Call of Duty Beta, you can drop into a Campaign mission before launch. “Entrenched” throws you into a large-scale assault as friendly forces race to prevent a strategically important power station from falling into enemy hands. Fight alongside armored vehicles and infantry while experiencing the cinematic action and core gameplay systems that define the Modern Warfare 4 Campaign, all accessible during the Beta.
...
## Player Progression (Multiplayer)
...
- Unlock new weapons, equipment, Perks, Field Upgrades, Killstreaks, and Beta Rewards by increasing your Player Level.
- Weekend One: Progress through Level 20 and unlock the first five Beta Rewards.
- Weekend Two: Reach Level 30 to unlock every gameplay item and all eight Beta Rewards.
- Unlocked Beta Rewards become available in the full game when Modern Warfare 4 launches on October 23.
...
Every match you play earns XP toward your Player Level (also known as Player Rank), steadily unlocking new ways to customize your Operator both cosmetically and tactically. Early progression expands your selection of Default Loadouts before Create a Class unlocks at Level 4, opening access to fully customized loadouts. Continue ranking up to unlock additional weapons, Equipment, Perks, Field Upgrades, Killstreaks, and eight Beta Rewards throughout the Beta.
...
- Track your Player Level and XP progress from the Multiplayer lobby and after every match via the After Action Report. Each new level immediately unlocks additional gameplay items, making it easy to see what's available next as you progress through the Beta.
- For a complete overview of your progression, open the main Multiplayer left Side Menu, select Career Profile (top left), then choose Progression. Here you can view your current Player Level, Rank, upcoming unlocks, and every item earned throughout the Beta.
...
Weekend One allows progression to Player Level 20, while Weekend Two raises the level cap to 30, granting access to the remaining gameplay unlocks and Beta Rewards. Cosmetic Beta Rewards earned during the Beta are tied to your Activision Account and will be available when Modern Warfare 4 launches, while gameplay progression resets when the Beta concludes.
...
PLAYER PROGRESSION TOP
...
- Unlock Create a Class immediately: New players begin with Default Loadouts. Reach Player Level 4 as quickly as possible to unlock Create a Class and start building your own custom loadouts.
- Check your Daily Challenges: Review your available Daily Challenges before deploying. Many can be completed together, helping you earn bonus XP and progress through the Player Levels more quickly.
- Keep an eye on your next unlock: Use the Progression screen to see exactly what's coming next. Knowing your upcoming weapon, Perk, Equipment, or Killstreak unlock can help you plan your next matches.
...
- Remember the weekend caps: Weekend One is capped at Player Level 20. Return for Weekend Two to continue progressing through Level 30 and unlock the remaining gameplay items and Beta Rewards. You can continue to play once you’ve hit the Player Level cap, you will just not be able to level up any further than each weekend’s cap. Earning XP once you’ve hit the Player Level cap will not go toward the second weekend.
...
